.SH NAME
omorfos\-keys \- keys.yaml, the keys of the omorfos desktop and what they do
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/omorfos/keys.yaml\fR, usually \fB~/.config/omorfos/keys.yaml\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The keys bound to actions, beside the built\-in bindings, and the built\-in bindings done without. \fBomorfosctl action\fR lists every action, with what it takes and what it does.
.PP
It is read again as soon as it is saved. If it has a mistake, its contents before are kept, and the mistake is shown among the notifications and printed by \fBomorfosctl config check\fR, with its line and column; the other files still apply.
.SH BUILT\-IN BINDINGS
.PP
There before anything is written, and kept unless \fBdefaults: false\fR is: a binding of yours on the same keys, or on keys that begin with them, takes the place of one, and \fBunbind\fR does without one.
