omorfos's settings, which are not there yet.
.RE
.TP
\fBbindings[].action.spawn\fR
A program to start with the session: its name and arguments, or that and what it may do.
.TP
\fBbindings[].action.spawn.may\fR
What it may do that an ordinary program may not.
.RS
.TP
\fBpanel\fR
Put surfaces on the screen outside windows and keep room for them, and list the windows.
.TP
\fBoverlay\fR
Cover the screen and take the keyboard while it does.
.TP
\fBlock\fR
Lock the session.
.TP
\fBask\fR
Show the prompt that asks for a secret.
.TP
\fBcapture\fR
Take pictures of the screen and of windows.
.TP
\fBclipboard\fR
Read and set the clipboard at any time.
.TP
\fBinput\fR
Type and click as the user, and see what is typed into fields.
.TP
\fBscreens\fR
Arrange the screens and change their colour.
.RE
.TP
\fBbindings[].action.spawn.run\fR
A program followed by its arguments, run without a shell.
.TP
\fBbindings[].action.stay_awake_for\fR
From 1 to 86400.
.TP
\fBbindings[].action.swap\fR
A half of the screen.
.RS
.TP
\fBleft\fR
The left half.
.TP
\fBright\fR
The right half.
.TP
\fBtop\fR
The top half, or upwards.
.TP
\fBbottom\fR
The bottom half, or downwards.
.RE
.TP
\fBbindings[].action.tile\fR
A half of the screen.
.RS
.TP
\fBleft\fR
The left half.
.TP
\fBright\fR
The right half.
.TP
\fBtop\fR
The top half, or upwards.
.TP
\fBbottom\fR
The bottom half, or downwards.
.RE
.TP
\fBbindings[].action.workspace\fR
From 1 to 32.
.TP
\fBbindings[].keys\fR
The keys to press, such as \fBSuper+Return\fR. Separate several chords with spaces to make a chain pressed one after another, such as \fBSuper+x t\fR.
.TP
\fBdefaults\fR
Which built\-in bindings are kept, on the keys these bindings leave alone: a Mac's, with Super for Command, unless this is \fBordinary\fR, for the ordinary way's with Ctrl and Alt, or \fBfalse\fR, for none.
.RS
.TP
\fBordinary\fR
.RE
.TP
\fBunbind\fR
Built\-in bindings to do without, by their keys, such as \fBSuper+h\fR.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
Three keys bound, one of them in place of a built\-in binding, and one built\-in binding done without:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
bindings:
  \- keys: Super+Return     # in place of the built\-in terminal
    action: { spawn: [foot] }
  \- keys: Super+l
    action: lock
  \- keys: Super+x t        # a chain: Super+x, then t
    action: { workspace: 2 }
unbind: [Super+h]          # a built\-in binding done without
.RE
.fi
